[
    {
        "content": "<p>How do you implement this without moving the <code>FnOnce&lt;()&gt;</code> out of box? I.e. in-place calling the function.</p>",
        "id": 631038065,
        "sender_full_name": "Boqun Feng",
        "timestamp": 1791818850
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For example a simple <code>into_inner()</code> implementation will cause a move IIUC.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">impl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">FnOnce</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KBox</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nb\">FnOnce</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">call_once</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arg</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">())</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">Output</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">into_inner</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">// Move occurs here</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 631043140,
        "sender_full_name": "Boqun Feng",
        "timestamp": 1791820070
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think <code>KBox</code> can do that, since the <code>self</code> in <code>FnOnce</code> is passed by-value</p>",
        "id": 631104364,
        "sender_full_name": "Benno Lossin",
        "timestamp": 1791837281
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>alloc::boxed::Box</code> might be able to with compiler magic</p>",
        "id": 631104394,
        "sender_full_name": "Benno Lossin",
        "timestamp": 1791837295
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, that's how I feel</p>",
        "id": 631104423,
        "sender_full_name": "Boqun Feng",
        "timestamp": 1791837304
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>but I might want to use that magic</p>",
        "id": 631104483,
        "sender_full_name": "Boqun Feng",
        "timestamp": 1791837322
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>Box</code> also might not have this, I'm not sure</p>",
        "id": 631104630,
        "sender_full_name": "Benno Lossin",
        "timestamp": 1791837380
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>in std the implementation is:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">#[stable(feature = </span><span class=\"s\">\"boxed_closure_impls\"</span><span class=\"cp\">, since = </span><span class=\"s\">\"1.35.0\"</span><span class=\"cp\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"k\">impl</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Args</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">FnOnce</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Args</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"nb\">Sized</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">Allocator</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">FnOnce</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Args</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">Box</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">Output</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">FnOnce</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Args</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">Output</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">extern</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"rust-call\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">call_once</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">Args</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">Self</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">Output</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">FnOnce</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Args</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">call_once</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I think compiler can somehow avoid the move of <code>*self</code> for <code>Box</code>, but probably it doesn't work for a customized Box?</p>",
        "id": 631106517,
        "sender_full_name": "Boqun Feng",
        "timestamp": 1791838027
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yeah <code>*</code> is special for box</p>",
        "id": 631106680,
        "sender_full_name": "Benno Lossin",
        "timestamp": 1791838094
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>also, you need unstable features to write the impl in the first place, right?</p>",
        "id": 631106803,
        "sender_full_name": "Benno Lossin",
        "timestamp": 1791838152
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, <code>fn_traits</code></p>",
        "id": 631106982,
        "sender_full_name": "Boqun Feng",
        "timestamp": 1791838226
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>but essentially, I guess I only need <code>KBox</code> has the same special treatment as <code>Box</code> that <code>*self</code> won't cause move.</p>",
        "id": 631107789,
        "sender_full_name": "Boqun Feng",
        "timestamp": 1791838491
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The <code>FnOnce() for Box&lt;dyn FnOnce()&gt;</code> impl uses <code>#![feature(unsized_fn_params)]</code> (to allow passing <code>dyn FnOnce()</code> directly as argument to <code>call_once</code>) together with the fact that rustc special cases <code>Box</code> to allow moving out of it (which because of <code>unsized_fn_params</code> will not actually copy the raw bytes).</p>",
        "id": 632593479,
        "sender_full_name": "bjorn3",
        "timestamp": 1792257806
    }
]